PART 7: BEST PRACTICES

================================================================================

Best Practice 1: Use Stable Unique Keys

Good:

{books.map(book => (

  <Book
    key={book.id}
    book={book}
  />

))}


Avoid:

{books.map(book => (

  <Book book={book} />

))}

Why?
STABLE KEY
    ↓
RELIABLE ITEM IDENTITY
    ↓
BETTER RECONCILIATION
    ↓
FEWER IDENTITY-RELATED UI PROBLEMS


================================================================================

Best Practice 2: Prefer IDs from Data

================================================================================

Good:

const books = [
  {
    id: 1,
    title: 'Book 1'
  },
  {
    id: 2,
    title: 'Book 2'
  }
];

{books.map(book => (

  <Book
    key={book.id}
    book={book}
  />

))}


Prefer this for dynamic lists over:

{books.map((book, index) => (

  <Book
    key={index}
    book={book}
  />

))}

Comparison
Data ID                  | Array Index
-------------------------|-----------------------------------
Belongs to item          | Belongs to current position
Usually stable           | Can change after reorder/delete
Better identity          | Can misrepresent item identity
Preferred for dynamic UI | Use cautiously


================================================================================

Best Practice 3: Keep map() Simple

================================================================================

Better:

{books.map(book => (

  <Book
    key={book.id}
    book={book}
  />

))}


Harder to maintain:

{books.map(book => (

  <div key={book.id}>

    <h2>{book.title}</h2>

    <p>{book.author}</p>

    <p>{book.price}</p>

    {/* More complex logic */}

  </div>

))}


As the mapped JSX grows, consider extracting it into a reusable component.

================================================================================

Best Practice 4: Extract Complex List Items into Components

================================================================================

Preferred:

{books.map(book => (

  <BookCard
    key={book.id}
    book={book}
  />

))}


Component:

function BookCard({ book }) {

  return (
    <div className="book-card">

      <h2>{book.title}</h2>

      <p>{book.author}</p>

      <p>${book.price}</p>

    </div>
  );
}

Benefits
Benefit
-------------------------
Reusable component
Cleaner parent JSX
Easier testing
Better organization
Easier maintenance


