PART 8: COMMON MISTAKES

================================================================================

Mistake 1: Missing key

Wrong:

{books.map(book => (

  <li>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


Typical warning:

Each child in a list should have a unique "key" prop.


Correct:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


================================================================================

Mistake 2: Using Index as Key for Dynamic Lists

================================================================================

Avoid when list identity/order can change:

{books.map((book, index) => (

  <li key={index}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


Prefer:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


================================================================================

Mistake 3: Using Random Values as Keys

================================================================================

Avoid:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={Math.random()}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


Prefer:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


================================================================================

Mistake 4: Arrow Function Formatting

================================================================================

This syntax is valid:

{books.map(book =>
  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>
)}


For multi-line JSX, parentheses are often easier to read:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}

Important
Without Parentheses | Valid for a single returned JSX expression
With Parentheses    | Often clearer for multi-line JSX


So this is a style/readability recommendation, not a syntax requirement.

================================================================================

Mistake 5: Complex Logic Inside map()

================================================================================

Harder to read:

{books.map(book => (

  <div key={book.id}>

    {book.title}

    {book.price > 10 ? (
      <p>Expensive</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Affordable</p>
    )}

    {book.rating > 4 ? (
      <p>Highly Rated</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Good</p>
    )}

  </div>

))}


Cleaner:

{books.map(book => (

  <BookCard
    key={book.id}
    book={book}
  />

))}

Why?
Easier to read.
Easier to maintain.
Better organized.
Keeps list rendering simple.

================================================================================

COMMON MISTAKES - QUICK TABLE

================================================================================

Mistake              | Avoid                | Better
---------------------|----------------------|--------------------------
Missing key          | <li>...</li>         | <li key={book.id}>
Dynamic index key    | key={index}          | key={book.id}
Random key           | key={Math.random()}  | key={book.id}
Very large map JSX   | Complex JSX in map() | Extract BookCard
